{"title":"Career Roadmap · Maritime Lawyer","role":"Maritime Lawyer","summary":"A Maritime Lawyer, also known as a Shipping Lawyer or Admiralty Lawyer in relevant contexts, advises shipowners, shipping companies, cargo owners, insurers, ports, logistics companies, shipbuilders, charterers, banks and other maritime businesses on legal issues arising from shipping and marine commerce.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law - LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Aviation / Space / Maritime Law"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Maritime Lawyer, also known as a Shipping Lawyer or Admiralty Lawyer in relevant contexts, advises shipowners, shipping companies, cargo owners, insurers, ports, logistics companies, shipbuilders, charterers, banks and other maritime businesses on legal issues arising from shipping and marine commerce."},{"type":"p","text":"The field combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maritime law"},{"text":"Commercial law"},{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"International law"},{"text":"Insurance"},{"text":"Transportation law"},{"text":"Admiralty jurisdiction"},{"text":"Dispute resolution"},{"text":"Environmental regulation"},{"text":"Trade and logistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical matters include ship financing, charterparties, cargo claims, marine insurance, vessel registration, collisions, salvage, maritime liens, port operations and shipping disputes."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated LL.B","Maritime / Shipping Law Specialisation","Shipping / Maritime Law Internship","Junior Maritime Lawyer / Legal Associate","Shipping & Maritime Associate","Senior Associate","Maritime Law Specialist","Partner / Legal Head / Maritime Counsel"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative in-house pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law Graduate","Legal Executive – Shipping","Legal Counsel","Senior Le